      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When I refer to \"traditional polish\" and gravitas, I am referencing the subtle cues often associated with elite corporate culture, such as established pedigree and a measured delivery. Sterling's background implies comfort and fluency within established hierarchies, which translates well to deferential yet authoritative boardroom settings. Arjun and Marcus's backgrounds suggest a more hands-on or community-focused drive, which can sometimes be perceived as less *formally* calibrated for a highly traditional, board-level audience. This often relates to presentation cadence, vocabulary choices, and an inherited comfort level with high-stakes formality.",
      "source": "target",
